              <tr><td>Early oxidation</td><td>Slight colour darkening</td><td>TAN rise 0.1–0.3 mg KOH/g above baseline; RPVOT &gt; 50% of new oil</td><td>Low — monitor closely</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Moderate oxidation</td><td>Visible colour change; first varnish deposits</td><td>TAN rise &gt; 0.5 mg KOH/g; viscosity +10–15% above specification; RULER antioxidant depletion 30–60%</td><td>Medium — plan oil change</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Advanced oxidation</td><td>Dark oil; filter plugging; valve stiction</td><td>TAN rise &gt; 1.0 mg KOH/g; viscosity &gt;15% above spec; sludge deposits visible; metals elevated</td><td>High — change immediately</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Severe degradation</td><td>Black oil; equipment symptoms; bearing wear</td><td>TAN &gt; 2.0+ mg KOH/g; high insoluble content; XRF metals significantly elevated</td><td>Critical — investigate root cause</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

